## What problem(s) does this PR solve?

Speeds up all `Array` and `Dictionary` operations that need to convert, by taking a shorter round trip.
No behavior change expected.

## Additional information

The previous path called `can_convert_strict` 3 times, iterated constructors, and ended up in the same conversion functions anyway:

- `Variant::construct`
- ... calls `VariantConstructor`
- ...calls `VariantCaster`
- ... calls `p_variant.to<T>()`
- ...calls `operator T()`
- ... which again switches on the input type

### Benchmarks

> **Note:** benchmarks were written by AI.

Most converting operations are around ~10% faster (like `set`, `push_back` and `merge`).
`append_array` is around 80% faster when converting.

